            <div xml:id="d239">

                <pb facs="0313" n="247" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg247"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.01/390: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Costa Rica</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Sack</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">San
                                José</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-01-22T14:00:00-06:00">January 22, 1934—2
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:45 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4. Costa Rican Government has invited Trueblood<anchor n="22" xml:id="d239-f1"/>
                    and myself to official dinner Tuesday night, January 23rd, in honor Salvadoran
                    special mission. In light of telegram No’. 1 of January 12, 5 p.m.,<anchor
                        n="23" xml:id="d239-f2"/> signed Phillips, information requested immediately
                    as to whether desirable we should accept.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sack</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
